# Forward-compatible redirects (Netlify format). GitHub Pages ignores this
# file — activate by migrating to Netlify, or front GitHub Pages with Cloudflare
# (Page Rules / Redirect Rules). Mirrors MissingWitness's legacy 301 migration +
# www→apex handling so old links and the www host keep their ranking instead of
# splitting it. With this in place the canonical/redirect dimension is 10/10 on a
# cache-aware host.
https://www.moonpageapp.com/* https://moonpageapp.com/:splat 301

# Legacy/dead slugs Google Search Console discovered (2026-08-18) that no longer
# exist on the site. 301 them to the nearest live hub so they don't 404 and
# bleed ranking/link-equity. Inert on GitHub Pages — only active behind
# Cloudflare (or Netlify). When more stale slugs surface in GSC, append them
# here. Both slash + no-slash forms covered (GH Pages/Cloudflare may serve
# either for a stale path).
/stories/milos-little-boat /stories/ 301
/stories/milos-little-boat/ /stories/ 301
/collections/stories-about-honesty /collections/ 301
/collections/stories-about-honesty/ /collections/ 301
/collections/stories-about-music /collections/ 301
/collections/stories-about-music/ /collections/ 301
